    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d456">

                <pb facs="0623" n="549" xml:id="pg549"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.51/71</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-20T11:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 20, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11.50 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6779. Your 5139, July 12, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d456-f1"/> Mr. Balfour has handed me the long financial
                    statement by the Chancellor of the Exchequer which follows and which he requests
                    me to telegraph for the Secretary of the Treasury and the President. A copy goes
                    also by pouch. The financial situation has caused greater fear and depression
                    than has before been felt from any cause since the war began.</p>
                <p>All that follows this is Mr. Bonar Law’s
                    memorandum.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
